<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<pnml xmlns="http://www.pnml.org/version-2009/grammar/pnml">
  <net id="SEQ-07d" type="http://www.pnml.org/version-2009/grammar/ptnet">
    <name><text>07d Payment and settlement: how money moves from the Treasury Single Account to the payee (Modified Disbursement System)</text></name>
    <page id="page1">
      <place id="p1"><name><text>start</text></name><initialMarking><text>1</text></initialMarking></place>
      <place id="p2"><name><text>p2</text></name></place>
      <place id="p3"><name><text>p3</text></name></place>
      <place id="p4"><name><text>p4</text></name></place>
      <place id="p5"><name><text>p5</text></name></place>
      <place id="p6"><name><text>p6</text></name></place>
      <place id="p7"><name><text>p7</text></name></place>
      <place id="p8"><name><text>p8</text></name></place>
      <place id="p9"><name><text>p9</text></name></place>
      <place id="p10"><name><text>p10</text></name></place>
      <place id="p11"><name><text>p11</text></name></place>
      <place id="p12"><name><text>p12</text></name></place>
      <place id="p13"><name><text>p13</text></name></place>
      <place id="p14"><name><text>p14</text></name></place>
      <place id="p15"><name><text>end</text></name></place>
      <transition id="t01"><name><text>1. DBM to Servicing banks: NCA: limit for the MDS sub-account of the agency</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t02"><name><text>2. Accounting unit: Books: debit Cash-MDS, Regular, credit Subsidy from National Government. Registry of the NCA. No official receipt is issued for an NCA</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t03"><name><text>3. Cash unit to Servicing banks: Payment order (LDDAP-ADA) in three copies and summary list (SLIIE) in two, on paper or through the electronic facility of the bank</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t04"><name><text>4. Accounting unit: Books, on the day of the daily report: credit Cash-MDS, Regular</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t05"><name><text>5. Servicing banks: Check the payment order and the NCA balance. Debit the MDS sub-account (the NCA balance decreases)</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t06"><name><text>6. Servicing banks to Suppliers and payees: Direct credit, not earlier than 24 hours and not later than 48 hours after receipt</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="tau1"><name><text>end of: Payee has an account in the same bank</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t07"><name><text>7. Servicing banks to Suppliers and payees: Bank transfer. The payee bears the bank charge</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="tau2"><name><text>end of: Payee has an account in another bank</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t08"><name><text>8. Servicing banks to BTr: One copy of the summary list and of the payment order on the same day: notice of the amount to be replenished</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t09"><name><text>9. BTr to BSP: Instruction to replenish the servicing bank</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t10"><name><text>10. Treasury Single Account to Servicing banks: Debit the Treasury account, credit the account of the bank at BSP</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t11"><name><text>11. BTr: Books of the Treasury: debit Subsidy to NGAs, credit Cash in Bank</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t12"><name><text>12. Servicing banks to Cash unit: Validated copy of the payment order. Items that could not be credited are marked</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t13"><name><text>13. Accounting unit: For an item not credited: journal entry to cancel it, and a new payment order. Each month: reconcile the books with the bank statement of the sub-account</text></name></transition>
